	<tag>
		<name>authorizedUrl</name>
		<tag-class>
			com.crh.logon.taglib.AuthorizedUrlTag
		</tag-class>
		<body-content>JSP</body-content>
		<description>
			Only valid WITHIN an AuthorizationTag. Returns the url of the functionality, which is first authorized
			for the user. Has a role if the url has to be set according to the first accessible functionality.
			naturally not required within the authorization tag, but can be used to get the first valid, available url.
		</description>
	</tag>
	
	<tag>
		<name>defaultFallback</name>
		<tag-class>
			com.crh.logon.taglib.fallbacklogic.DefaultFallBackLogicTag
		</tag-class>
		<body-content>JSP</body-content>
		<description>
			Example: Unloading time of silos: if it is not set, and a shipto is defined for that, in db null must be used, but on the ui, the default value
			has to be shown disabled (value: the shipto's default, or if it is not available the logon default). The tag renders the input field
			and a checkbox 'from logon default'. The checkbox drives the input field's value in a meaning if it is checked it will be updated according to
			the default value and be disabled.
			Generally:
			This tag determines the object's default value according to the fallback logic. If one places a defaultFallBackInputField
			between the tag's delimiters it will lay out an input field rendered according to the fallback logic (in case it was retrieved by
			a fallback logic it will be disabled, and shown the value disabled, in case it has own value it will be editable and contains its
			normal value. The DefaultFallbackChexkbox will update the inputfield's value according to the fallback default value. (Let it enabled
			if the value comes from the object itself, disable it, if the object does not have such a value, and it has to use some level fallback
			default.
			 
		</description>
		<attribute>
			<name>objectName</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				Name of the pageContext object, which is in fact taken as a base of determining the own/fallback values. If not used, specify at least propertyValue
				which is usually the form's field.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>objectName2</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				Name of the pageContext2 object, which is in fact taken as a base of determining the own/fallback values. If not used, specify at least propertyValue
				which is usually the form's field.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>propertyName</name>
			<required>true</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				See constants of the tag class. The tag can be used to lay out these default values.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>propertyCheckboxName</name>
			<required>true</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				Name of the checkbox, the checkbox will be rendered with this name. Id will correspond with the name.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>propertyInputFieldName</name>
			<required>true</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				Name of the inputField, which will be used as the source of setting the object's property value. (For example in case of loadingpoint
				the name of the String field, which will be mapped to the loading point's loading time.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>propertyValue</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				In case the value is not really stored in the object, but on a form element, one can pass the value
				here as if it would be set to the object. In case it is a bad value, the fallback will not happen, the value will be layed out.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>readOnly</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				In case this is set, and true, the inputfield's value, and the checkbox's value will only be shown as text and not editable field.
			</description>
		</attribute>				
	</tag>

	<tag>
		<name>defaultFallbackInputField</name>
		<tag-class>
			com.crh.logon.taglib.fallbacklogic.DefaultFallBackLogicInputFieldTag
		</tag-class>
		<body-content>JSP</body-content>
		<description>
			Renders an input field with the name given in defaultFallback tag, which must surround the two 
			elements: the checkbox and the input field. (defaultFallbackInputField, defaultFallbackCheckbox)
		</description>
		<attribute>
			<name>style</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				Style, will be rendered as style attribute of the input field.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>maxLength</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				Maxlength, will be rendered as maxlenght attribute of the checkbox.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>styleClass</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				Class, will be rendered as class attribute of the input field.
			</description>
		</attribute>	
	</tag>

	<tag>
		<name>defaultFallbackCheckbox</name>
		<tag-class>
			com.crh.logon.taglib.fallbacklogic.DefaultFallBackLogicCheckboxTag
		</tag-class>
		<body-content>JSP</body-content>
		<description>
			Renders a checkbox with the name given in defaultFallback tag, which must surround the two 
			elements: the checkbox and the input field. (defaultFallbackInputField, defaultFallbackCheckbox)		
			Use only if there is an input field. See description of defaultFallback,defaultFallbackInputField Tags.
		</description>
		<attribute>
			<name>style</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				Style, will be rendered as style attribute of the checkbox.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>styleClass</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				Class, will be rendered as class attribute of the checkbox.
			</description>

		</attribute>
	</tag>
	
	<tag>
		<name>url</name>
		<tag-class>com.crh.logon.taglib.URLTag</tag-class>
		<body-content>JSP</body-content>
		<description>
			Adds a version label to a URL.
		</description>
		<attribute>
	        <name>var</name>
	        <required>false</required>
	        <rtexprvalue>false</rtexprvalue>
	    </attribute>
	    <attribute>
	        <name>scope</name>
	        <required>false</required>
	        <rtexprvalue>false</rtexprvalue>
	    </attribute>
	    <attribute>
	        <name>value</name>
	        <required>true</required>
	        <rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
	    </attribute>
	    <attribute>
	        <name>context</name>
	        <required>false</required>
	        <rtexprvalue>false</rtexprvalue>
	    </attribute>
	    <attribute>
	        <name>type</name>
	        <required>false</required>
	        <rtexprvalue>false</rtexprvalue>
	    </attribute>
	</tag>
	
	<tag>
		<name>wagonNumberFormat</name>
		<tag-class>com.crh.logon.taglib.WagonNumberFormatTag</tag-class>
		<body-content>JSP</body-content>
		<description>
			Prints out the input string, or the input wagonentity's number in the standard way.
		</description>
		<attribute>
	        <name>wagonNumber</name>
	        <required>false</required>
	        <rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
	         <type>java.lang.String</type>
	    </attribute>
	    <attribute>
	        <name>wagon</name>
	        <required>false</required>
	        <rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<type>com.crh.logon.persistence.entities.common.WagonEntity</type>
	    </attribute>
	</tag>
	<tag>
		<name>orderRowspan</name>
		<tag-class>
			com.crh.logon.taglib.OrderRowSpan
		</tag-class>
		<body-content>JSP</body-content>
		<description>
			Skips the body in case the id of the current item corresponds with the previous item.
			Otherwise prints out a td tag with the rowspan corresponding with the number of rows which had the same order id.
		</description>
		<attribute>
			<name>pageContextOrderList</name>
			<required>true</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<type>java.util.List</type>
			<description>
				The name of the list containing OrderCreateEntities.
			</description>
		</attribute>						
		<attribute>
			<name>pageContextOrderCreateEntityName</name>
			<required>true</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				The name of the current OrderCreateEntity.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>pageContextIndexName</name>
			<required>true</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				The name of the index.
			</description>
		</attribute>		
		<attribute>
			<name>printInTd</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				Write in this parameter if you want something to be printed in the td tag itself (such as style, id or whatever).
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>printTdTag</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				By default it is true, and it will print the surrounding td tag. If you just want to skip the content of the tag
				in case it corresponds, set false, and no td tag will be printed.
			</description>
		</attribute>		
	</tag>
	<tag>
		<name>dtOrderWrapperRowspan</name>
		<tag-class>
			com.crh.logon.taglib.DateTimeAwareOrderRowSpan
		</tag-class>
		<body-content>JSP</body-content>
		<description>
			Skips the body in case the id of the current item corresponds with the previous item.
			Otherwise prints out a td tag with the rowspan corresponding with the number of rows which had the same order id.
		</description>
		<attribute>
			<name>pageContextOrderList</name>
			<required>true</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<type>java.util.List</type>
			<description>
				The name of the list containing OrderCreateEntities.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>pageContextOrderCreateEntityName</name>
			<required>true</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				The name of the current OrderCreateEntity.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>pageContextIndexName</name>
			<required>true</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				The name of the index.
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>printInTd</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				Write in this parameter if you want something to be printed in the td tag itself (such as style, id or whatever).
			</description>
		</attribute>
		<attribute>
			<name>printTdTag</name>
			<required>false</required>
			<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
			<description>
				By default it is true, and it will print the surrounding td tag. If you just want to skip the content of the tag
				in case it corresponds, set false, and no td tag will be printed.
			</description>
		</attribute>
	</tag>
		<tag>
		<name>evaluateIfDisabled</name>
		<tag-class>com.crh.logon.taglib.OrderDetailButtonLogicTag</tag-class>
		<body-content>JSP</body-content>
		<description>
			Evaluates the tag's body in case the buttonFunc operation is not allowed for the user/order. See the Tag class what buttonFunc are involved.
		</description>
		<attribute>
	        <name>buttonFunc</name>
	        <required>true</required>
	        <rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
	    </attribute>
		<attribute>
	        <name>orderObjName</name>
	        <required>false</required>
	        <rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>	        
	    </attribute>	    	    	    
	</tag>	
  <tag>
    <name>formatDateWithUserTimezone</name>
    <tag-class>com.crh.logon.taglib.FormatDateWithUserTimezoneTag</tag-class>
    <body-content>JSP</body-content>
    <description>
      Format date AsDayMonthYearHourMinute with the timezone of user
    </description>
    <attribute>
          <name>date</name>
          <required>true</required>
          <rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
          <type>java.util.Date</type>
      </attribute>
  </tag>
</taglib>
